# y6: top-ups for shorter y-guides
def _top(slug, para, faq):
  t, ps = LONG[slug]; ps=list(ps); LONG[slug]=(t, ps[:-1]+[para]+ps[-1:]); FAQX[slug]=list(FAQX[slug])+[faq]
_top('18x24-album-size-guide',"Before committing a whole album to 18x24, print one sample sheet and hold it the way the client will. Large formats impress in the studio but can feel unwieldy at home, so a sample helps clients choose with confidence.",("Is 18x24 more expensive to print than 12x36?","Per sheet it is usually similar or higher because of the larger area and board size. Ask your lab for a per-sheet quote."))
_top('puberty-ceremony-album-design',"Finally, agree the delivery date early. Families often want the album ready for a follow-up function or for relatives visiting from abroad, so plan design and lab time backwards from that date and leave a week for revisions.",("How long does it take to design a puberty ceremony album?","With photos selected, a 20 to 25 sheet album typically takes two to four working days, plus lab time and one or two revision rounds."))
_top('anniversary-album-design-ideas',"Leave a final page or two free of photos for handwritten messages from children and grandchildren. Many families treasure these more than any design, and it turns the album into a keepsake the whole family has contributed to.",("How long before the anniversary should I start the album?","Start at least four to six weeks ahead to allow time for collecting and scanning old photos, design, revisions and printing."))
_top('haldi-mehendi-album-pages',"Plan the order of photos within each chapter to follow the event as it happened: setup and details first, then the bride or groom, then family joining in, then the celebration. A natural sequence makes even playful pages easy to follow, and it helps relatives relive the day in order.",("Should haldi pages come before mehendi in the album?","Follow the order in which the events happened at that wedding. In many families mehendi comes first, in others haldi does, so confirm with the couple."))
_top('wedding-album-captions-and-quotes',"When in doubt, leave it out. A beautiful spread with no text is always better than one with a generic line that adds nothing.",("Should every spread have a caption?","No. Most spreads look better without text; keep captions for chapter openers and a few key moments."))
_top('parents-album-design-guide',"Finally, consider how parents will show the album. Many will open it for visiting relatives for years, so durable lamination, a sturdy cover and a box or bag are worth recommending. Matte finishes hide fingerprints from frequent handling, and a slightly smaller size is easier to pass around a room full of guests.",("Can parents' albums be printed at the same time as the main album?","Yes, and it is usually more efficient. Send all albums to the lab as one order with clearly separated folders."))
_top('album-binding-and-lamination-guide',"Whatever you choose, keep a written note of the binding, finish and board thickness for each client so reprints and parents' copies match the original exactly.",("Can I mix lamination finishes within one album?","Most labs apply one finish to all sheets, though some allow a different finish on the cover. Ask your lab."))
_top('album-design-client-revisions',"Remember that clear communication is part of the product. Clients who understand the process feel more confident, give better feedback and are more likely to recommend you to friends planning their own weddings. A short, friendly explanation of how proofs and revisions work, sent at the start of every project, sets the tone for the whole album.",("Should I charge for extra revision rounds?","Many studios do, at a fixed fee per round, once the agreed rounds are used. State this clearly in your initial agreement."))
